I reported a cardinal-rule violation between enemies.js (maxHp:100000) and
boss_hp_override.json (666666) and "fixed" it by syncing the override down
to 100000. That was backwards.

App.jsx getScaledMaxHp (~5209) SPECIAL-CASES Lucifer and returns a flat
333,333 per phase / 666,666 total, with no deck hpScale and no boss-kill
reduction. Confirmed at seven sites in App.jsx. The maxHp:100000 field in
enemies.js is DEAD DATA for Lucifer — nothing reads it for the real fight.
So 666666 was the true value and the sim's own hardcode at :1488 already
matched live. There was never a divergence.

Consequences of the bad "fix":
  - it silently made the JSON disagree with the live fight
  - a later balance experiment took the same wrong turn, cut Lucifer to
    185,000 (3.6x easier than shipped) and reported a 24.5% win rate that
    was pure artifact. Retracted.

Both sync gates now EXEMPT Lucifer and assert it against 666666 instead:
vestibule-sim-kwstacks.js assertBossHpSync and e2e/test-card-parity.cjs.
The parity gate mattered urgently — it exits 1 on a CORRECT repo, which
would have failed run-tests.bat and blocked the whole rig.

Also guarded an unguarded reduce in devils_wager (:1341) that threw
"Reduce of empty array" when every member was already Too Stoned —
roughly 1 run in 90,000.

Verified: parity gate passes across all 27 enemies; 20,000-game sim runs
clean at 4.46% Lucifer / 3.42 strikes per fight.

